# Generated output. Prettier reformatting a build artifact is work that the
# next build throws away, and it makes `format:check` depend on whether a
# build has happened since the last format.
dist/
.astro/
pnpm-lock.yaml
# .astro components are handled by `astro check`/eslint, not prettier
# (no prettier-plugin-astro installed).
*.astro
# The documentation content is Markdown in an MDX envelope, and markdownlint
# owns it. Prettier reflowed a fenced code block nested in a <TabItem> onto its
# own opening fence line, which rendered the quickstart's install tab as an
# empty code block; keeping both authorities on the same files made each
# formatter dirty the other.
src/content/docs/**/*.mdx
# Generated from the card registry by cmd/gen_layouts, byte for byte, and held
# to it by `make check-layouts`. Prettier puts a short array of fields back on
# one line, which means `pnpm run format` would rewrite this file and the next
# check-layouts would call it stale: two authorities over one file, and
# whichever ran last wins. The generator is the one that can be right.
src/data/layouts.json
